<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Builds a `section`_ for the resource :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**The implementation keeps ownership** of whatever it returns, for as long as the graph
built from it lives -- the graph only borrows its `sections`_ unless it was asked to
copy them (see :cpp:class:`IniSectionGraph`&apos;s own note)
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sectionName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name for the <computeroutput>section</computeroutput>_ </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The generated <computeroutput>section</computeroutput>_, or <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> to skip it </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
